# TheAuditor — line-ending policy
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AND WHY IT IS NOT OPTIONAL:
# Person A develops on Windows, Person B runs on a Linux ROCm instance.
# CanonicalDoc.source_text is BYTE-PRESERVED raw document text, and the
# verifier's `amounts_appear_in_source` check does substring matching against
# it. If git silently converts CRLF <-> LF on the way in or out, fixtures
# authored on Windows will behave differently on the GPU box, and the failure
# looks like an accuracy problem rather than a checkout problem.
#
# Policy: normalise source to LF; treat all DATA as binary so git never
# touches a byte of it.

# Source and docs: normalise to LF in the repo, checkout as LF everywhere.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.cfg   text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf

# DATA: never convert. These are ground truth and must survive round-trips
# byte-for-byte across operating systems.
*.json      -text
*.jsonl     -text
data/**     -text
runs/**     -text

# Windows scripts genuinely want CRLF.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf

# Binary assets
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.docx  binary
*.pptx  binary
